<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Resolve the repair-marker question (createdby vs impersonation) and verify live quick-create flags (spec Unresolved Q1, Q2)</title>
    <phase>5 W5 Records created outside the product</phase>
    <gate>019 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Read-only investigation producing notes; no code or schema change.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Bounded grep plus read-only Dataverse metadata reads.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W5-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>019</deps>
    <tags>investigation, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Answer two blocking questions with evidence and record the answers. (1) Does any product path create rows under impersonation (`MSCRMCallerID`), so that platform `createdby` ≠ BFF app user would wrongly select product-created rows? (2) What are the LIVE quick-create flags (`isquickcreateenabled`) for every mapping-target table, including Project, Matter and Invoice Line Item? Read-only: no live writes.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, Dataverse metadata, BFF identity model (ADR-028).</role>
  <goal>`notes/w5-open-questions.md` gives, for Q1, the final FR-25 selection-marker decision with file:line evidence, and for Q2, a per-table live flag table that fixes the FR-24 table list; `notes/decisions.md` carries a matching entry.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md "Unresolved Questions" (repair marker; live quick-create flags), FR-24, FR-25. Blocks the final FR-25 selection query (task 052) and the FR-24 table list (task 051). The solution XML says quick create is on for some tables while the architecture doc says off.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/w5-open-questions.md</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/decisions.md (append entry)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api (grep for MSCRMCallerID, CallerObjectId, impersonat in the Communication routes and create cores)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse (grep for MSCRMCallerID; Web API client header handling)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md (claims about quick create being off)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/spec.md FR-24, FR-25</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="019" status="pending">W2 deployed; the live create path is the one being characterised.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: environment access. Read-only. Use Dataverse MCP `describe` / `read_query` (see dataverse-mcp-usage skill); no create, update, publish or import against any environment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: identity findings. Report which principal is `createdby` for each BFF create route (user via OBO, app user, impersonated). Do not change auth code; any change is a separate escalated task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: deliverable. Output is notes only; no code. If Q1 shows impersonated product creates, propose the alternative marker in the note and escalate rather than implement.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse createdby vs createdonbehalfby; quick create metadata</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/data.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="web-api-client" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/web-api-client.md">Where the Web API client sets caller headers.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare STANDARD rigor; read spec Unresolved Questions, FR-24, FR-25.</step>
    <step order="1">Q1: grep `MSCRMCallerID`, `CallerId`, `createdonbehalfby`, impersonation helpers across `src/server`; for every create route that writes a mapping-target or standard-owned table, record which principal Dataverse stamps as `createdby` (user OBO vs BFF app user). Conclude whether `createdby` ≠ BFF app user is a safe "created outside the product" marker, and for which tables.</step>
    <step order="2">Q2: with Dataverse MCP `describe`, read `IsQuickCreateEnabled` (and the quick-create form presence) for every mapping-target table (derive the list from the registry in spec/design, including sprk_project, sprk_matter, sprk_invoicelineitem, sprk_event, sprk_todo, sprk_workassignment, sprk_analysis, sprk_communication, sprk_document, memo/KPI tables). Tabulate live vs solution XML vs architecture-doc claim.</step>
    <step order="3">Write `notes/w5-open-questions.md` (answers, evidence, residual risk) and append a `decisions.md` entry stating the FR-25 selection marker and the FR-24 table list.</step>
    <step order="4">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="5">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any product create path runs under impersonation or stamps `createdby` as a non-app principal such that product rows would match the repair selection, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the proposed alternative marker.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a table's live quick-create flag differs between environments, record each and ask the owner which governs the FR-24 list.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Overlaps with notes/decisions.md, which records only the decision, not the evidence tables.</existing>
    <extension>decisions.md gets the one-line decision; the per-route and per-table evidence is too large to inline there (spec §11). This is a project note, not product surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without recorded evidence, tasks 051 and 052 would build the FR-24 table list and the FR-25 selection query on unverified assumptions (spec Unresolved Q1, Q2).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools><tool name="dataverse-mcp">describe / read_query for metadata (read-only)</tool><tool name="grep">Source search</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/w5-open-questions.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/decisions.md (entry)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`w5-open-questions.md` states, with file:line evidence per create route, which principal is `createdby` and gives a final yes/no verdict on `createdby` ≠ BFF app user as the FR-25 marker.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note has a per-table live quick-create table covering every mapping-target table including Project, Matter and Invoice Line Item, each with live value, solution-XML value and doc claim.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`decisions.md` has an entry that resolves both Unresolved Questions and names the final FR-24 table list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no write, publish or import was performed against any environment (statement and the list of read calls in the note).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note and decision entry exist and are committed-ready; no source files changed.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec Unresolved Q1 (repair marker) and Q2 (live quick-create flags). Unblocks tasks 051 and 052.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
